# ─── Paths ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Absolute path to the brain/content directory where all data is stored.
# Default: ../../brain/content  (relative to backend/, resolves to repo root)
# Set this only if you want to keep data outside the repo.
# VAULT_PATH=/absolute/path/to/brain/content

# Working directory for the terminal and for managed OpenCode sessions.
# It becomes the v2 session location, so repository exploration is scoped to
# this project rather than the backend directory. Default: repo root (two
# levels above backend/).
# WORK_DIR=/absolute/path/to/repo

# ─── Server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port the backend listens on.
# Default: 3001
# PORT=3001

# ─── Local AI runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app never stores provider keys. Authenticate the CLI locally, then choose
# one runtime. `none` preserves every non-AI Life OS feature.
AI_RUNTIME=none

# Codex: sign in with `codex` before selecting this runtime.
# CODEX_COMMAND=codex
# CODEX_MODEL=

# OpenCode: setup/chat can explicitly start a managed OpenCode 2.x server after
# a user click. It is always `opencode serve --hostname 127.0.0.1 --port ...`;
# Life OS creates an ephemeral OPENCODE_PASSWORD in backend memory and never
# writes or renders it. Do not add that password or provider credentials here.
# Provider credentials stay in OpenCode's own config/auth.
# Managed launch requires this exact IPv4 loopback HTTP shape with a fixed port.
# A manually started legacy v1 server remains supported as an external endpoint,
# but Life OS never adopts, restarts, or stops it.
# OPENCODE_COMMAND=opencode
# The Life OS setup/chat session bridge intentionally uses this exact model.
# OPENCODE_MODEL=assistant/assistant
# OPENCODE_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4096

# Origins allowed to issue explicit terminal, managed-server, and OpenCode
# pairing actions in Life OS. Comma-separated only when the Vite UI is
# deliberately hosted elsewhere.
# LIFE_OS_UI_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# ─── Google Calendar (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables two-way sync with Google Calendar.
# Setup: https://console.cloud.google.com → Create project → Enable Calendar API
#        → OAuth 2.0 credentials → Desktop app
#
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3001/api/sync/auth/callback
# GOOGLE_TIMEZONE=Europe/Moscow
